  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nThere's currently two different ways to create \"buttons\" in HTML, one being `<button>` and one being `<input type=\"button\">` (/reset/submit). The input button pre-dates the \"real\" button element and has a number of limitations that the button element does not (e.g. It has layout limitations, can't have rich content, and doesn't support command/commandfor).\n\nShould we mark input buttons as obsolete?",
